Hi all,
Ahead of the upcoming discussion, I wanted to share a summary of the key areas that, based on the discussions to date, I believe would benefit from further clarification. Understanding the end-to-end architecture and deployment model will be important in answering these questions.
1. IBM OSO image onboarding and supply chain
The IBM OSO images are not currently following the standard 3PIIP ingestion path. How the end-to-end process from ingestion through scanning, storage and deployment, including how the necessary controls and approval gates are applied.
2. Internally built s390x images
The project is also developing its own s390x images, while the current LSE toolchain does not support s390x. How the tactical approach for this project works and the longer-term direction, including ownership and approval of the build pattern, and how controls are applied across build, scanning, promotion, image integrity and traceability.
3. Deployment, runtime security and observability
Where and how the workloads will run and what security, runtime and observability controls are available within that environment. 
4. Vulnerability management and reporting
How vulnerabilities identified across both IBM-supplied and internally built images will be identified, tracked, remediated and reported through the appropriate vulnerability management lifecycle.
